[statement]
A `!` entry the walk follows leads it to a package to be removed that
carries or provides its name, at whatever version, and apk removes it
there: `x`, which `y` needed through `v`, a name `x` provides at a version,
would be removed last
(`a-package-needed-through-a-name-it-provides-at-a-version-is-removed-last`),
but `b` states `!x>5`, and apk removes `x` as its walk follows that entry,
before installing `b`.

[repository]
P:b
V:1
D:!x>5

[installed]
P:x
V:1
p:v=1

P:y
V:1
D:v

[request]
b

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
remove y 1
remove x 1
install b 1
